    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "A major question in human evolutionary history has been whether humans left Africa in one migration or multiple migrations that eventually resulted in establishment of populations in other continents. While recent genome-wide studies have determined that East Asian and Oceanian populations likely arose from the same Out-Of-Africa (OoA) migration, the genetic relationship between Southeast Asian populations and their geographical neighbors remains unclear. Analysis of modern and archaic human genomes shows that Oceanian populations shared ancestry with Denisovans, possibly due to interbreeding events that occurred in Southeast Asia before those humans migrated into the Sahul. Based on patterns of single nucleotide polymorphism variation in the genomes of modern day humans, Neanderthals, and Denisovans, I estimate the phylogenetic relationships among the populations in these geographical areas and their divergence times using genomics analysis programs such as Treemix and BEAST. This research clarifies Southeast Asian population history, taking into account divergence times between Oceanian and East Asian populations and estimates of Denisovan ancestry. I found that modern Southeast Asian populations are primarily descended from migrants from East Asia who migrated into Southeast Asia quite recently, likely corresponding to the spread of rice farming agriculture after 9,000 years ago.  However, genetic traces remain of earlier inhabitants of Southeast Asia, who descend from the populations with Denisovan ancestry, producing descendants who migrated into Sahul and gave rise to modern day Aboriginal Australian, Papuan, and Near Melanesian populations. By elucidating Southeast Asian divergence and admixture history, we can more accurately characterize when and how humans migrated out of Africa to found modern human populations in the rest of the world.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
